hw/audio/es1370: accept register accesses narrower than 32 bits

The Ensoniq Windows driver programs the chip byte- and word-wise, and the memory core passes such accesses to the device unaligned.
Until now they all fell into the default case: writes were dropped and reads returned all ones, so the DAC stayed at 5512 Hz and the codec always looked busy.
Adds trace points for the control, status, serial control and codec registers, interrupts and the default cases.

Apply inside a QEMU 9.2.x source tree: patch -p0 -i ../fixes/qemu92x-es1370-subword-access.patch

